export anchor SpaceAge1960sStyle:
    number: 141
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Space age 1960s
    idea: The dashboard is a filled in mission control form on white paper, with numbered fields, embroidered style patches, T minus countdown clocks for due dates and GO, HOLD, SCRUB status.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #f7f5ef, the page
        form: #ffffff, the form sheet and fields
        ink: #141414, text, form rules and patches
        graphite: #555149, field labels
        rule: #b9b4a8, inner rules and the planned path
        grid: #e6e1d4, graph paper
        orange: #e8590c, top stripe, trajectories and this week bars, never small text
        burntOrange: #b33f00, field numbers, the primary button and times
        console: #161a1d, countdown clock faces
        digit: #ff8a3d, clock digits and the focus halo
        earthBlue: #2a5d8f, the insignia globe only
        goGreen: #1d6b3a, On track
        holdAmber: #8a5300, At risk
        scrubRed: #b3261e, Behind and overdue
    type:
        Extended head type uses Eurostile, Microgramma, Michroma, Bank
        Gothic, Helvetica Neue at 800. Body uses Helvetica Neue, Helvetica,
        Arial. Mono uses SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas. Readouts 48px, greeting
        30px, mission names 17px, clocks 18px mono, body 14px, field labels
        10px caps tracked 0.16em with a burnt orange field number.
    layout:
        An orange stripe tops a white header with a round orbit insignia,
        Program office over the spaced brand, a boxed search with a ruled
        label cell, a burnt orange New project, a square bell and Flight
        director Mara Okafor, over ruled nav cells with the current one
        black with an orange base. A Mission status report title with a
        form number leads into one ruled form sheet. Its first row holds
        field 01 with the greeting, date and a red Hold box, then fields 02
        to 05 as big readouts. Six mission cells follow in three columns,
        each with a round patch and initials, numbered category, name, an
        orange trajectory arc over a dashed planned path, a field grid of
        tasks and percent with a black T minus clock, and a status row. The
        last row holds a Communications transcript and Fig. 1, a graph paper
        bar chart with outline bars for last week and orange bars for this.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 14 to 16px inside form cells, cells abut on shared rules.
    density: Dense like paperwork. One form sheet holds every section.
    corners: Square forms and buttons, round patches and insignia, 4px clocks.
    borders: A 1px ink form grid, a 4px orange top rule, 1px light rules inside mission fields.
    shadows: None.
    icons: Filled circle with check On track GO, framed pause bars At risk HOLD, solid cross Behind SCRUB, each with the word and a boxed code.
    focus: A 2px ink outline offset 2px inside a 6px digit orange halo.
    tone: Program office formal, such as Mission status report, Flight director, Communications transcript, Fig. 1 and Hold.
